        "Content": "Egans are delighted to present Rathlevanagh House to the open rental market. Rathlevanagh House is a quintessential Irish country farmhouse dating from circa 1888, combining period charm with modern comfort. This superbly presented, private detached residence is accessed via electric security gates, offering exceptional privacy in a highly desirable and convenient location. \r\n\r\nThe property is set within large, beautifully landscaped gardens, which will be maintained by the owner. Accommodation on the ground floor comprises an entrance hallway, office, spacious open-plan kitchen/living area, utility room, dining room, and sitting room. The entire ground floor benefits from underfloor heating. On the first floor, there are four generous double bedrooms, including a master bedroom with en-suite and walk-in wardrobe, along with a family bathroom. The owners have meticulously maintained this exceptional home, which is presented in excellent condition throughout and comes to the market fully furnished. Outside, there is a two-storey garage with an electric roller door. The ground floor offers practical storage space, including a dedicated area for storing logs, while the upper level provides flexible space ideal for storage, hobbies, or recreational use.\r\n\r\nRathvelanagh is ideally situated with direct access to the N4 Dublin to Sligo roadway, the property provides effortless connectivity while retaining a tranquil countryside setting. The home is also just minutes from the scenic shores of Lough Owel, renowned for its natural beauty, recreational amenities, and peaceful surroundings. The property is located approximately 9 kilometers west of Mullingar town centre. Mullingar is a thriving and well-regarded town, increasingly attractive to commuters and those with fully remote or hybrid working arrangements. Fibre broadband is available, and the town is serviced by the Dublin to Sligo railway line, offering excellent transport connectivity.\r\n\r\nMullingar to Dublin is commutable in under one hour via the N4 and M4 roadways, while Dublin International Airport is approximately 75 kilometres away, making national and international travel highly convenient. Mullingar, the main county town of Westmeath, offers a vibrant nightlife and music scene. For anglers and outdoor enthusiasts, there are three neighbouring lakes, Lough Owel, Lough Ennell, and Lough Derravaragh, all renowned for their natural beauty and excellent fishing. The town provides an excellent choice of primary and secondary schools, including St Finian's College, Loreto College, nearby Wilson's Hospital School, Coláiste Mhuire Mullingar, and Mullingar Community College. For schools further afield, Clongowes Wood College and Our Lady’s Bower are within a 45-minute drive, while Dublin schools are also easily accessible. For leisure and outdoor pursuits, Mullingar Golf Course, Belvedere House and Gardens, Tullynally House and Gardens, Mullingar Equestrian Centre, and Kilbeggan Racecourse, are all within easy reach. Strictly no pets. Viewing of this exceptional property is highly recommended with Egans."
      },
